  "id": "COMPOUND:19392 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether is shown to have a target relationship with SCCH-26 through multiple pathways, with the primary target being Macrophage scavenger receptor types I and II. These receptors are targeted by two different compounds: 7-Hydroxy-6-(2-(R)-Hydroxy-3-Methylbut-3-Enyl)Coumarin and 3,8-Dihydroxy-9-methoxypterocarpan, both of which also target SCCH-26. Additionally, Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether is linked to MIP, which is targeted by Cycloeudesmol, which in turn targets SCCH-26. The integration of these pathways suggests a potential mechanism by which Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether may influence SCCH-26 through the modulation of macrophage scavenger receptors, possibly by interfering with the uptake or signaling of ligands that bind to these receptors. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Islandicin 4-Methyl Ether and SCCH-26, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on SCCH-26 indicates a plausible biological pathway, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship.",
